// Links the cortiq inference runtime (Rust staticlib from the cmf
// release) into Runner, so DynamicLibrary.process() can find the C ABI.
//
// Three settings are load-bearing, and dropping any one of them puts the
// app back on the demo engine WITHOUT failing the build:
//
//   -force_load pulls every member of the archive in, but on its own it
//   is not enough: nothing in the Swift/ObjC side references the engine
//   (the Dart side looks it up at runtime), symbols of a static library
//   are not exported from an executable by default, and -dead_strip then
//   removes the whole runtime as unreachable. Measured: a probe linked
//   this way comes out at 84 KB and dlsym finds nothing.
//
//   -exported_symbol _cortiq_* makes those symbols roots, which both
//   keeps the code and puts it in the export trie dlsym reads.
//
//   Accelerate resolves _cblas_sgemm, which the engine's Apple-platform
//   sgemm path calls. The link only used to succeed without it because
//   the code that needs it was being stripped away.
//
// Metal and friends are what the runtime's wgpu backend needs from
// cortiq-ffi 0.5.31 on; without them the link fails on undefined Metal
// symbols. IOSurface and CoreGraphics come in through wgpu's surface
// support, which is linked in even though inference only ever computes.
OTHER_LDFLAGS[sdk=iphoneos*] = $(inherited) -force_load $(PROJECT_DIR)/Frameworks/libcortiq_ffi.a -Wl,-exported_symbol,_cortiq_* -framework Accelerate -framework Metal -framework Foundation -framework QuartzCore -framework CoreGraphics -framework IOSurface
// Simulator slice (aarch64-apple-ios-sim), built locally; without it the
// simulator falls back to the demo engine.
OTHER_LDFLAGS[sdk=iphonesimulator*] = $(inherited) -force_load $(PROJECT_DIR)/Frameworks/libcortiq_ffi_sim.a -Wl,-exported_symbol,_cortiq_* -framework Accelerate -framework Metal -framework Foundation -framework QuartzCore -framework CoreGraphics -framework IOSurface
// The sim slice is arm64-only (Apple Silicon hosts).
EXCLUDED_ARCHS[sdk=iphonesimulator*] = x86_64 i386
// The archive is stripped after linking, and Xcode's default style for an
// app ("all") empties the export trie again — symbols exported above,
// gone by the time the IPA is written, dlsym back to nothing. Stripping
// local symbols only keeps the exports and still drops the debug names.
STRIP_STYLE = non-global
